Subject: mkmod writes rank: a root-class disk controller's sd class

Contract C4-1 section 4.1, C4-2 section 1.  A root-class disk controller
declares its sd rank class in its Master ($rank z3660, zorro, mobo or
ide); mkmod's key loop left it out, so .moddata had no rank= and the
core refused the module's sd_register with EINVAL.  The z3660scsi port
found it.  mkmod now writes $rank like $match.

--- a/tools/mkmod
+++ b/tools/mkmod
@@ -9,8 +9,8 @@
 #   Driver.o   the module's code (any number of objects linked into it)
 #   Master     "$depend a b ..." lines (any number), "$modtype misc|drv|str"
 #              (the wrapper macro's type; misc when absent),
-#              the .moddata v2 keys as "$class boot|demand", "$cpu 68020"
-#              (required), "$match", "$majors", "$unload", "$tier",
+#              the .moddata v2 keys as "$class root|boot|demand", "$cpu 68020"
+#              (required), "$match", "$rank", "$majors", "$unload", "$tier",
 #              "$build", "$desc" (one each) and "$param" (any number),
 #              and a final line "name prefix flags ..." ('#' comments)
 #   Space.c    optional, compiled and linked in
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@
 	echo "	.asciz	\"cpu=$CPU\""
 	echo "	.asciz	\"class=$CLASS\""
 	[ -z "$DEPEND" ] || echo "	.asciz	\"depend=$(echo $DEPEND | tr ' ' ',')\""
-	for k in match majors unload tier build desc; do
+	for k in match rank majors unload tier build desc; do
 		v=$(key $k)
 		[ -z "$v" ] || echo "	.asciz	\"$k=$v\""
 	done
